<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Tserclaes, Count of Tilly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1559">1559</a>–<a href="/years/1632">1632</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Tserclaes, Count of Tilly, was a Walloon general who commanded the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>. He won victories at the White Mountain in 1620, Wimpfen in 1622 and Lutter in 1626, and his army's sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a> in 1631 became notorious. Defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-breitenfeld-1631">Breitenfeld</a> in 1631, he was fatally wounded at the Lech in 1632.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-tserclaes-count-of-tilly.jpg" alt="Johann Tserclaes, Count of Tilly" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Tserclaes_count_of_Tilly.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Christian IV’s intervention in the Thirty Years’ War ended in defeat by <b>Tilly</b> at Lutter am Barenberge in 1626.</blockquote><a href="/empire/denmark-norway">Denmark-Norway · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Maximilian I built a disciplined standing force, founded the Catholic League in 1609 and, with its general Count <b>Tilly</b>, shared in the Catholic victory at the Battle of White Mountain near Prague in 1620.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-bavaria">Duchy of Bavaria · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>His army was destroyed at the Battle of White Mountain on 8 November 1620, Spanish troops under Spinola occupied the left bank, and in 1622 the Catholic League's army under <b>Tilly</b> took Heidelberg.</blockquote><a href="/empire/electoral-palatinate">Electoral Palatinate · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Christian IV won the Kalmar War of 1611–1613 but was beaten by <b>Tilly</b> at the Battle of Lutter am Barenberge in 1626 during the Thirty Years’ War, and the Torstenson War ended in the losses of the Treaty of Brömsebro in 1645.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-denmark">Kingdom of Denmark · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>At Breitenfeld (1631), Swedish and Saxon forces routed <b>Tilly</b>'s veteran Catholic League army, and at Lützen (1632) the Swedes held the field against Wallenstein even though Gustavus himself was killed.</blockquote><a href="/empire/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Near Rain in Bavaria, a Swedish army under Gustavus Adolphus defeated the Catholic League force of <b>Johann Tserclaes, Count of Tilly</b>, in the Thirty Years' War.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-15">15 April in history</a></li></ul></section>
